  "lawGrade": "MAPPED",
  "lawGradeScale": "v4 law grading scale (native canon scale, strongest first): DERIVED, LOCKED, MAPPED, PARTIAL, SPLIT, OPEN, DEFINITIONAL. Mapping to C0-C6 unruled - tracked as OI-0011.",
  "statementTechnical": "Newtonian gravitation F = -GMm/r^2 with angular momentum L gives the effective potential V_eff(r) = -GM/r + L^2/(2r^2). For L != 0 a stationary point exists: bounded orbits are possible - the system remains in structured relationship with the source. For L = 0 there is no stationary point: monotone infall, collapse into the source without distinction. The mapping identifies L with relational engagement (response / worship): grace is always attractive, and orbit - closeness with preserved distinction - requires what the creature brings. Angular momentum is conserved: what you bring to the relationship is preserved.",
  "statementPlain": "Gravity always pulls and never pushes, but whether you orbit or crash depends on what you bring. Bring angular momentum and you hold a stable orbit - close enough to be warmed, far enough to remain yourself. Bring nothing and you fall straight in. The proposed reading: grace always draws, and relationship needs your response to keep it from collapsing into sameness. The physics is established; the grace mapping is proposed, not proven - it remains an open structural analogy, not a demonstrated identity.",
  "mathematicalForm": "V_eff(r) = -GM/r + L^2/(2r^2); L != 0 => stationary point (bounded orbit); L = 0 => monotone infall",
  "mathFormNormal": "V_eff(r) = -GM/r + L^2/(2r^2); L != 0 => stationary point (bounded orbit); L = 0 => monotone infall",
  "masterEquationVariables": [
    "G"
  ],
